1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:01,960
Whoever gets there and touches 
the statue’s hand first

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:03,280
gets to take the BTS.

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:03,880
Deal?

4
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:10,480
Someone like Bay is just going to 
keep messing with me.

5
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:12,480
If I want this to end,

6
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,040
settling it with a competition is the right way.

7
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,200
You used to play tennis?

8
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:17,760
I did.

9
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,600
But that was over ten years ago.

10
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,000
How good were you?

11
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:22,200
Are you gonna wipe the floor with Sun?

12
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,480
You're comparing me to him.

13
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:24,880
He's making the national team.

14
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,320
Then why'd you sign up?

15
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,600
Since he's leaving,

16
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,040
before he goes,

17
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,840
I want to mess with him one last time.

18
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,320
Why do you hate him so much?

19
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,880
Honestly,

20
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,320
I don't really hate him.

21
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,200
The match wasn't fair.

22
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,320
You should play again.

23
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:42,240
How wasn't it fair?

24
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:43,400
Hey, enough.

25
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:45,480
Bay won fair and square

26
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:49,160
Congratulations.

27
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:00,120
Hey.

28
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,400
Come down here,

29
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:07,840
loser.

30
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:09,520
Stay right there.

31
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:10,360
I’m coming down.

32
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,720
Just wait, asshole.

33
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,160
Hurry up and come down.

34
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:18,400
Where are you?

35
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:19,680
What is it now?

36
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:29,640
(SAMING PHON FAI)

37
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,280
You coward.

38
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:49,280
(FOR YOUR SHOULDER,
BUT YOU'RE STILL A "LOSER")

39
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:04,720
Hey!

40
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,200
(S.SUNN_YT STARTED FOLLOWING YOU.)

41
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:06,880
(FOLLOW BACK)

42
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:07,880
You unblocked me?

43
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,000
(FOLLOWING)

44
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,160
Huh?

45
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,920
You hid all your childhood photos?

46
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:31,520
Shit!

47
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,200
(I SAW THAT!)

48
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:35,040
Shit!

49
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:39,840
Why are you so fast?

50
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:02,600
(FOR YOUR SHOULDER,
BUT YOU'RE STILL A "LOSER")

51
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:09,320
Hey.

52
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,280
What are you smiling about?

53
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,120
Bay!

54
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:55,760
Yes, Dad.

55
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:56,680
What are you doing?

56
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,320
Just scrolling on my phone.

57
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:02,920
Go buy me some shampoo and toothpaste.

58
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,040
We're almost out.

59
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,960
Why don't you ask Boat to go?

60
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,000
He's washing the dishes.

61
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,120
He should stay in the back.

62
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:12,840
You go.

63
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,120
Do me a favor.

64
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:19,400
I've been adding water to my shampoo
and shaking the bottle,

65
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,400
and now it won't even lather.

66
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,840
Go and come straight home.

67
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,040
Okay, Dad.

68
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:23,520
Good.

69
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,120
You practice on weekends too?

70
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:18,880
Why the hell are you asking?

71
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:20,800
I always practice on weekends.

72
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,360
Hey.

73
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,600
I was just being friendly.

74
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:25,760
You're the one who wanted a truce,

75
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:26,880
and this is how you talk to me?

76
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,600
What exactly do you want?

77
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:32,680
You're taking the BTS, right?

78
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:34,560
I'm heading that way

79
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,640
to buy some things for my dad.

80
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:36,280
Coming?

81
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,120
Hey.

82
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,520
Don't think too hard.

83
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:43,760
So?

84
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:44,720
Coming?

85
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:47,080
Hurry up, it's hot.

86
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:50,480
Yeah.

87
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,200
Fine.

88
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:53,160
Hop on then.

89
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:54,400
Come on.

90
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,560
You're Sun, right?

91
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,000
at the last PREMS' GAME.

92
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,960
You were amazing

93
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:26,520
You were playing against my school,

94
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:27,960
but I was rooting for you.

95
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:28,960
Wow!

96
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:29,920
Really?

97
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:30,560
Yeah.

98
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,440
Thanks a lot.

99
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,360
Boy Seriously.

100
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,160
I'm thinking of signing up this year.

101
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,440
Maybe I'll get to compete against you.

102
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:36,920
I'd love to play tennis with you.

103
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,040
Umm...

104
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:45,400
What the hell?

105
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:47,600
Why?

106
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,080
Am I not allowed to stand here?

107
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,120
Does your dad own this town?

108
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:55,000
What the hell is wrong with you?

109
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:56,520
I'll get going.

110
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:59,200
But could I take a photo with you?

111
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:00,200
Oh, sure.

112
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:00,760
Really?

113
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:05,480
Could you take a pictureof me and Sun?

114
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:11,120
Of course.

115
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,160
Thank you.

116
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,160
Wow.

117
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,440
Take a good one.

118
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,600
Make sure he looks handsome.

119
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,440
You're so freaking cool!

120
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:25,840
Check the photos.

121
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,240
Umm.

122
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:28,280
I can take them again if you want.

123
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,880
Are they okay?

124
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,440
Yeah, yeah.

125
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,800
I'd better get going.

126
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,720
Oh, I'll tag you.

127
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:37,600
I've been following you for ages.

128
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:38,280
Thanks.

129
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:38,960
Yeah.

130
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,160
What's the rush?

131
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,040
Was that boy hitting on you?

132
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:49,480
Huh?

133
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,400
No.

134
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,640
I'm just a legend.

135
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,680
People always ask for my Instagram

136
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:56,800
or want a photo with me

137
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:57,720
whenever I go to practice.

138
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,240
If that's hitting on me,

139
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:03,200
then I've got dozens of people doing it.

140
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,120
Oh, yeah?

141
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,920
And did you give them your Instagram?

142
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:08,280
Of course.

143
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:11,280
They DM me to ask for tennis tips.

144
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,040
Wanna see?

145
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,080
Where is it?

146
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:17,760
Oh, wow, look...

147
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:20,160
Like ten, twenty people.

148
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:20,640
See?

149
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:22,720
Here...

150
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:25,200
All these DMs.

151
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,240
Hmm.

152
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:27,320
Hey!

153
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,480
Why'd you do that?

154
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,040
(DID HE DM YOU?)

155
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:58,720
(YEAH.)

156
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:15,920
(HE ASKED ME IF YOU WERE MY BOYFRIEND.)

157
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:16,920
(SO FUNNY.)

158
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,960
(WHY'D YOU TAKE A SELFIE?)

159
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,320
You're so freaking cool!

160
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:33,640
Check the photos.

161
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:34,760
Umm.

162
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:35,800
I can take them again if you want.

163
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,320
Are they okay?

164
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:39,000
Yeah, yeah.

165
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,440
(Well, I got annoyed.)

166
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,720
(You can clear things up yourself.)

167
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:48,880
(Nah.)

168
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,840
(I don't feel like talking to him anyway.)

169
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,160
Don’t go to the practice today.

170
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,240
After school, come straight home.

171
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,160
And don't put too much strain 
on your shoulder.

172
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:29,680
Papa,

173
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,320
you don't have to remind me.

174
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,160
I know that.

175
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:34,800
Papa,

176
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:38,320
don't close the restaurant tomorrow morning

177
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:41,840
just to drive me here.
I had business around here anyway.

178
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:43,280
Go. 

179
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,400
Go on to class.

180
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:46,720
Yes, Papa.

181
00:11:47,880 --> 00:11:48,480
See you.

182
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:54,800
I'm off.

183
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,160
Oh, hey,

184
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:17,520
Did you hear Sun lost a tennis match?

185
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,320
To be honest,

186
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:22,360
I think Sun is not even that good.

187
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,200
He’s just overrated.

188
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:26,760
I'd be so embarrassed.

189
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:28,120
He's about to become a professional athlete,

190
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,440
and he lost to a nobody.

191
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:33,960
So what if he lost to me?

192
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:37,520
How about this?

193
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:39,840
If you think he's not that good,

194
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,280
why don't you challenge him yourself

195
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:43,480
instead of talking sh*t behind his back?

196
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:44,920
Go on.

197
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:51,160
Get out of here.

198
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:54,880
Focus on your study.

199
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:25,360
Thank you.

200
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:30,720
Hey.

201
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:32,800
You don't have to thank me.

202
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,200
Those guys just pissed me off.

203
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,520
Instead of complimenting my skills,

204
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:41,200
they were talking sh*t about you.

205
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:43,280
It was so damn annoying.

206
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:08,200
Are you really doing this, Ken?

207
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,320
Have you thought it through?

208
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:11,040
Yes, sir.

209
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:13,200
I discussed it with my parents yesterday.

210
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:18,880
Okay.

211
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:20,640
Then I'll...

212
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,600
respect your decision, Ken.

213
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:31,560
Hello, sir.

214
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:32,920
Hello, sir.

215
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:34,160
Hello, Coach Kong.

216
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,000
I'll head back to class.

217
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:38,520
Goodbye, sir.

218
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:43,880
Actually,

219
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,200
you can just call me Kong, like before.

220
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:47,480
Of course not.

221
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,360
You're a teacher now.

222
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,400
And Sun's coach as well.

223
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,960
Oh, Sun...

224
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:54,920
I hardly have to coach him.

225
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:57,040
The coach you found for him

226
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,480
has already trained him very well.

227
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:00,800
Right.

228
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:03,560
So, how have things been for you?

229
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:07,680
Have you taken the school team

230
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:09,440
to any tournaments yet?

231
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,680
Won many trophies?

232
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:13,520
This is only my first year.

233
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:17,160
Right now, I'm still adjusting to the team

234
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,800
and recruiting new players.

235
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:20,160
Right.

236
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,480
Actually, I owe you an apology.

237
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:28,200
Sun's already competing in the youth circuit,

238
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:30,080
so he hasn't been able to compete for the school

239
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:31,920
and bring recognition to your club.

240
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:34,880
What can I do?

241
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:37,200
Actually, I...

242
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:42,000
wish I could help you win some trophies

243
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:46,200
and medals to put on display.

244
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:50,160
What do I have to do?

245
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,160
Hmm.

246
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:15,560
Amazing.

247
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:22,120
Hey, Bay.

248
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,040
Come on in.

249
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:25,600
Hi, Coach.

250
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,080
Can I help you?

251
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:29,000
I have something to tell you.

252
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:32,120
Hmm, perfect timing.

253
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,600
I have something to tell you too.

254
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:36,560
Umm, I think...

255
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:40,760
I'm going to have you play doubles.

256
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:47,080
Then who's playing singles?

257
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,320
I'll have Sun play singles.

258
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,320
He'll probably bring home a gold medal.

259
00:16:58,520 --> 00:16:59,360
(SAMING PHON FAI)

260
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,440
Come on, Bay.

261
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:01,760
Try to understand.

262
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:04,880
You...

263
00:17:05,760 --> 00:17:07,760
Sun asked you to do this, didn't he?

264
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:09,840
It's not like that, Bay.

265
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:11,360
You've got it all wrong.

266
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:13,640
The reason I'm putting you in doubles

267
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:16,160
is because I think it'll be easier for you.

268
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,480
And this is your first tournament.

269
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:20,360
That's fine.

270
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:22,360
Maybe it's for the best.

271
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,720
I was already thinking about 
withdrawing anyway.

272
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:26,120
If that's how it is,

273
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:27,200
I'm okay with it.

274
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,640
I'm not competing anymore.

275
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:30,000
Hey.

276
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:33,960
Damn it.

277
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,920
Honestly, I'm kind of sad.

278
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,480
I thought I'd be the first one
to leave the club.

279
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,320
Turns out it's you instead.

280
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,880
Have you told anyone yet?

281
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,080
Yeah.

282
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:45,600
I told Ming,

283
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:46,720
Coach Kong,

284
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:47,600
and you.

285
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,480
Since you've made up your mind,

286
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,800
you'd better become a judge.

287
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,480
Don't get ahead of yourself.

288
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:56,520
I don't even know if I'll get into college yet.

289
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,800
Anyway, take care of Ming for me.

290
00:17:59,400 --> 00:17:59,840
Hmm.

291
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:00,960
Me?

292
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:02,040
Yeah, you.

293
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,600
Now that you're not playing singles,

294
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,960
why don't you take my place?

295
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:07,560
Right.

296
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,440
By the way,

297
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,400
I think Bay's withdrawing.

298
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:12,840
Huh?

299
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:13,640
What do you mean?

300
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:16,000
Hey!

301
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:16,960
Hold on.

302
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:21,200
Hey!

303
00:18:21,760 --> 00:18:22,280
Hey!

304
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:23,720
Hey!

305
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:28,040
Have you withdrawn yet?

306
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,160
If you haven't, don't.

307
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:32,200
Ken's not playing doubles anymore.

308
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:36,040
Oh.

309
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,960
So it really was you
who talked to Coach Kong.

310
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:41,880
Are you really an athlete?

311
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:44,240
What the hell are you talking about?

312
00:18:45,560 --> 00:18:47,160
You couldn't accept losing?

313
00:18:49,560 --> 00:18:51,640
Have you no f*cking shame?

314
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:54,120
Son of a b*tch!

315
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:55,400
F*ck you!

316
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,240
Hey, calm down!

317
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:57,320
You guys, calm down!

318
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:15,200
What the f*ck is wrong with you?!

319
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:15,840
What are you muttering?

320
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,240
You're the one who threw the first punch.

321
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,040
F*ck you!

322
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:19,680
Quiet!

323
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:21,280
That's enough, okay?

324
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:23,720
Sun!

325
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:26,120
-Sun! Are you okay?
-Pa.

326
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:29,800
You're not a child anymore.

327
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,560
Is violence the only way
you know how to solve problems?

328
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:32,720
-Please, sir.
-Huh?!

329
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:33,480
Sir,

330
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:35,640
please don't use that kind of language.

331
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:37,400
Chun, you son of a b*tch!!

332
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:37,800
Dad!

333
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:39,200
Oh, my.

334
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:41,880
Did Sun do this to you?

335
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:42,520
Ouch!

336
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:44,040
It hurts!

337
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:46,800
Is this how you raise your son?

338
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:48,240
Teaching him to solve everythingwith violence?!

339
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:49,960
Wasn't it your son who started it?

340
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:50,280
Look!

341
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,440
Look at my son's face.

342
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:51,880
See?

343
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:53,920
Bay!

344
00:19:56,640 --> 00:20:00,000
Didn't your son provoke mine first?

345
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,400
My son was just defending himself.

346
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:03,200
How can you even say that?

347
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:05,600
-Your son started it!
-Please, sir.

348
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:06,960
-Sir.
-Is this how you raised your son?

349
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:08,800
Wonder where he learned it from?

350
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,640
Sir, please stop.

351
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:12,560
Hello.

352
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:14,120
-Hello, Principal.
-Hello.

353
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:15,720
Hello.

354
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:18,680
Principal, please be fair to my son.

355
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:20,160
I understand.

356
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:22,920
First, I'd like to speak to each side separately.

357
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,960
Bay and Bay's father, please come in.

358
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:27,840
Please.

359
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:29,560
Bay.

360
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:37,640
Pa, look.

361
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,480
Any more bruises?

362
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:44,040
So, you were upset because Coach Kong

363
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:45,320
assigned you to doubles

364
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:48,280
even though you won the singles tryout, right?

365
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,200
Yes, ma'am.

366
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,640
Here's what I don't understand.

367
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:54,040
What does Sun have to do with it?

368
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:57,160
Sun asked Coach Kong to get rid of me

369
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:59,960
because he wanted to play singles himself.

370
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:01,320
I don't know anything about that, ma'am.

371
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:02,880
I never spoke to Coach Kong about it.

372
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:06,040
Bay's just making excuses.

373
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,680
Actually, he told me yesterday

374
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,480
he was going to withdraw.

375
00:21:12,840 --> 00:21:13,920
Withdraw?

376
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,240
You were going to withdraw, Bay?

377
00:21:17,280 --> 00:21:18,360
That was the plan, Dad.

378
00:21:18,800 --> 00:21:19,960
Hey, don't do that.

379
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,320
Why would you quit?

380
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:24,120
I'm sorry, ma'am.

381
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:26,200
The thing is,

382
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:31,520
my son won the tryouts fair and square.

383
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:34,640
So he deserves to stay in the tournament,

384
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:35,840
isn’t that right, ma’am?

385
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:36,840
Actually,

386
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:38,000
I can play doubles instead.

387
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:40,440
Quiet, Sun.

388
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:42,640
Coach Kong must have decided

389
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:43,760
that putting you in singles

390
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:44,160
gave the school a better chance

391
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,720
of winning a medal.

392
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:46,880
Now that I think about it,

393
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:49,880
it must have been Coach Kong's own decision.

394
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:51,080
Isn't that right, ma'am?

395
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:54,160
At lunch today,

396
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,680
I went into Coach Kong's office,

397
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:58,800
and I saw him eating dim sum from Sun's place.

398
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,960
If Sun hadn't spoken to him,

399
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:03,120
where would that dim sum have come from?

400
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:08,240
And don't tell me Coach Kong ordered

401
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,600
dim sum from their place.

402
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:12,440
He just ordered from my restaurant.

403
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:15,440
Why would he order from theirs too?

404
00:22:15,680 --> 00:22:16,800
Isn't that right, ma'am?

405
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:20,680
Umm, yes.

406
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:24,960
This morning, Sun’s father brought me some dim sum.

407
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,760
And he did suggest you something, didn’t he?

408
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:34,840
Normally, this would be serious enough

409
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:35,760
to get you fired.

410
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:39,920
But since this is your first offense,

411
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:41,320
I’ll just give you a warning.

412
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:44,040
Thank you, Principal.

413
00:22:44,560 --> 00:22:45,440
But there will still be disciplinary action.

414
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:46,160
Your salary will be docked

415
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,280
so the other teachers won’t follow your example.

416
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:54,920
Because of what happened,

417
00:22:56,520 --> 00:22:57,640
it wasn’t fair to Bay.

418
00:22:58,080 --> 00:22:58,920
There.

419
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:01,400
You heard that?

420
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:05,880
You have to be fair to my son.

421
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:10,600
But you shouldn’t have said that to your friend, Bay.

422
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:11,200
Oh.

423
00:23:11,480 --> 00:23:12,040
That’s true.

424
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:17,360
You have to be fair to my son too.

425
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,160
I have made up my mind.

426
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:22,400
Next week, once both of you have fully recovered,

427
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:25,240
I’ll have Coach Kong hold another tryout

428
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:26,640
just for Sun and Bay.

429
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:30,760
Another tryout?

430
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:32,680
But we have to submit the players’ names

431
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,400
to the tournament organizers now.

432
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:34,880
I’ll talk to them myself.

433
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:37,280
Either way,

434
00:23:37,280 --> 00:23:38,480
you were also at fault in this matter, Coach Kong.

435
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:40,080
We’ll talk later, privately.

436
00:23:41,040 --> 00:23:41,880
Are you two okay with this?

437
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:48,760
If you say so,

438
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:50,440
I don’t mind.

439
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:53,440
I don’t mind, either.

440
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:54,880
Whatever you say, ma'am.

441
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,640
I was asking the boys.

442
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:02,760
I’m okay with that, ma’am.

443
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:04,600
Whatever you say.

444
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:09,720
Sun!

445
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:12,000
Answer the Principal.

446
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:18,200
If that’s how it has to be,

447
00:24:21,040 --> 00:24:22,040
I don’t have any problem.

448
00:24:24,760 --> 00:24:25,720
Okay.

449
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:27,320
So that’s over.

450
00:24:28,040 --> 00:24:29,000
You’re okay with that, sir?

451
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:30,800
Everything is clear now, sir?

452
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:32,320
In that case,

453
00:24:32,760 --> 00:24:35,000
thank you for your time coming down here.

454
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:35,920
-Of course, ma’am.
-Of course, ma’am.

455
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:38,600
Thank you so much.

456
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:42,440
Let’s go, Pa.

457
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:43,920
Hold on, Sun and Bay.

458
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:47,320
-Yes, ma’am?
-Don’t leave yet.

459
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:50,760
Since you two caused all this trouble today,

460
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:54,120
after school, you’ll clean the bathrooms

461
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:55,200
as punishment.

462
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:59,120
Eh? Why am I getting punished too?

463
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:00,880
It’s a punishment.

464
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:02,720
But he started it.

465
00:25:03,440 --> 00:25:05,120
You both caused the trouble,

466
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:06,280
so you’ll both be punished together.

467
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:06,880
Okay?

468
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:10,480
Just help each other.

469
00:25:22,760 --> 00:25:24,800
I’d like to apologize again.

470
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,520
Next time, don’t listen to him.

471
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:29,080
You’re so annoying.

472
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:30,680
The principal has solved the problem.

473
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:31,440
Just stop talking.

474
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:34,280
I’m not gonna waste my time arguing with you.

475
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:36,000
Then shut your mouth.

476
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:38,640
You just keep talking.

477
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:39,640
Dad.

478
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:45,680
How was it, dad?

479
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:47,920
What do you want now?

480
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:49,120
What else do you want?

481
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:49,680
Huh?

482
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:52,400
Damn it.

483
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,040
Is Bay hurt badly?

484
00:25:55,880 --> 00:25:56,680
We’ll talk at home.

485
00:25:57,080 --> 00:25:58,280
But I have to say,

486
00:25:58,560 --> 00:26:00,800
Sun’s face is more messed up.

487
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:10,480
Boat,

488
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:14,800
you’re not gonna say hi to me?

489
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,840
Aren’t you the reason my brother’s in trouble?

490
00:26:23,240 --> 00:26:25,040
Well, I didn’t know it would turn out like this.

491
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,080
Yeah, I know you.

492
00:26:31,600 --> 00:26:32,320
Don’t worry about it.

493
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:34,120
I’m off.

494
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:36,160
Boat,

495
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:40,480
are you avoiding me?

496
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:42,680
You didn’t reply to any of my texts.

497
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:46,440
Nah, why would you say that?

498
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:49,400
I’ve been busy with my studies.

499
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:51,040
That’s all.

500
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:55,120
I’ll text you when I have time, okay?

501
00:26:57,680 --> 00:26:58,160
See you.

502
00:27:08,280 --> 00:27:09,000
What, dad?

503
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:11,920
What were you two talking about?

504
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,280
Just saying hi to my friend.

505
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:19,560
Does Kong know about you?

506
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:23,080
How would he know?

507
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:26,200
Good. Keep it that way.

508
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:34,600
Slow down.

509
00:27:59,240 --> 00:27:59,560
Look.

510
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:06,440
I didn’t know my dad went to talk
with the coach.

511
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:11,520
Why are you telling me now?

512
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:16,080
Because I want you to know

513
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:18,120
that I’m not trying to sabotage you.

514
00:28:23,600 --> 00:28:24,480
If you really think that,

515
00:28:25,040 --> 00:28:25,720
why don’t you go tell the principal

516
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:26,840
to put me back in the competition?

517
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:30,320
Didn't you say you were going to withdraw?

518
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:33,000
I wasn't going to withdraw

519
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:34,040
because I thought I couldn't do it.

520
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:36,320
I was going to withdraw

521
00:28:37,040 --> 00:28:37,680
so I wouldn't keep showing up

522
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,320
and getting on your nerves.

523
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:44,280
Let me ask you this.

524
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:47,520
You think if I continue with the competition,

525
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:49,400
I wouldn’t win, right?

526
00:28:55,320 --> 00:28:57,120
In the end, you think you're better than everyone else.

527
00:28:58,840 --> 00:28:59,720
Assh*le.

528
00:29:01,280 --> 00:29:01,640
Hey.

529
00:29:02,880 --> 00:29:04,320
What the f*ck is wrong with you?

530
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,480
Why did you sign up in the first place?

531
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:13,800
Answer me.

532
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:16,840
Why did you start playing tennis again?

533
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:20,400
Why are you competing with me?

534
00:29:20,680 --> 00:29:21,800
How does that matter?

535
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:22,880
It f*cking matters.

536
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:26,960
You show up whenever you like,

537
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:30,040
and you leave whenever you want, right?

538
00:29:34,200 --> 00:29:36,200
You never change at all.

539
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:42,520
Back then,

540
00:29:44,080 --> 00:29:46,000
I begged you to keep playing with me,

541
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:47,680
but you didn’t even care.

542
00:29:53,840 --> 00:29:54,560
Back then?

543
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:01,280
I’m not gonna play tennis with you anymore.

544
00:30:28,480 --> 00:30:28,920
Right.

545
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:31,520
I do think I’m better than you.

546
00:30:35,760 --> 00:30:36,360
At least,

547
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:40,480
I kept my promise from that day.

548
00:30:42,520 --> 00:30:44,040
I never stopped playing tennis.

549
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,120
But you’re the one

550
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:54,640
who gave up.

551
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:57,240
You still remember that day?

552
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:00,800
Hey.

553
00:32:14,040 --> 00:32:15,040
What, honey?

554
00:32:18,800 --> 00:32:20,680
Did it bother you that much?

555
00:32:52,040 --> 00:32:52,840
(At least,)

556
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:55,440
(I kept my promise from that day.)

557
00:32:56,280 --> 00:32:57,960
(I never stopped playing tennis.)

558
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,640
(But you’re the one)

559
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:00,800
(who gave up.)

560
00:33:39,360 --> 00:33:40,240
(The rooftop.)

561
00:33:52,640 --> 00:33:53,720
Have you calmed down?

562
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:57,280
You're calling me hotheaded?

563
00:33:58,080 --> 00:33:58,360
Hey.

564
00:33:59,040 --> 00:33:59,880
I didn't say that.

565
00:34:00,760 --> 00:34:01,440
Just hear me out.

566
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:07,680
I'm sorry.

567
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:12,800
Sorry for what?

568
00:34:15,320 --> 00:34:16,560
I'm sorry I punched you.

569
00:34:19,320 --> 00:34:19,840
That's it?

570
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:20,360
Wait!

571
00:34:21,040 --> 00:34:22,080
I'm sorry...

572
00:34:24,120 --> 00:34:24,920
about what happened back then.

573
00:34:30,520 --> 00:34:31,440
Why?

574
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:33,640
Actually...

575
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:37,840
I still remember what happened.

576
00:34:51,960 --> 00:34:52,680
Chun.

577
00:34:54,640 --> 00:34:56,640
Looks like you and I had the same idea.

578
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,440
I was just about to come see you.

579
00:35:00,280 --> 00:35:01,160
I was so frustrated

580
00:35:01,200 --> 00:35:02,160
-I couldn't sleep.
-Pa!

581
00:35:03,840 --> 00:35:05,400
We still have unfinished business.

582
00:35:05,400 --> 00:35:06,440
Let's settle it once and for all.

583
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:08,080
I couldn't sleep either.

584
00:35:08,680 --> 00:35:09,920
Probably for the same reason.

585
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:12,160
Just tell me what you want.

586
00:35:14,160 --> 00:35:15,760
Now that your son and my son

587
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:19,640
are competing fairly,

588
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:22,520
-I think we should...
-Just get to the point.

589
00:35:22,880 --> 00:35:24,120
Let's make a deal.

590
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:25,720
Whoever's son loses,

591
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:26,800
that family shuts down their shop.

592
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:27,600
Huh?!

593
00:35:28,520 --> 00:35:29,120
Yeah.

594
00:35:29,400 --> 00:35:30,800
That's exactly what I was going to say.

595
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:32,480
Let's put it in writing.

596
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:33,680
BE Fine.

597
00:35:33,920 --> 00:35:34,520
Deal.

598
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:38,880
-Deal.
-You draw up the contract,

599
00:35:38,960 --> 00:35:41,200
and I'll come over tomorrow to sign it.

600
00:35:44,760 --> 00:35:46,920
One of us will have to find a new profession.

601
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:49,440
You should sell noodles.

602
00:35:49,440 --> 00:35:50,640
Or fish dumplings.

603
00:35:50,640 --> 00:35:52,560
That seems more your style.

604
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:56,000
Sh*t!

605
00:35:57,400 --> 00:35:58,200
Oh, f*ck!

606
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:03,240
What are we gonna do?

607
00:36:03,440 --> 00:36:04,680
Go talk to your dad.

608
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:06,680
Make him forget about this.

609
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:08,680
You talk to your dad.

610
00:36:09,080 --> 00:36:10,160
My dad's too stubborn.

611
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,400
Yours is easier to talk to.

612
00:36:12,720 --> 00:36:14,640
My dad's stubborn too.

613
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:16,440
Your dad's easier.

614
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:17,680
If you don't talk to him,

615
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,360
one of our families will have to move.

616
00:36:22,440 --> 00:36:23,600
Are you really okay with that?

617
00:36:24,320 --> 00:36:25,960
Of course not.

618
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:34,680
You mean that?

619
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:44,400
Hey!

620
00:37:00,360 --> 00:37:01,840
I don't want you to leave either.

621
00:37:21,400 --> 00:37:23,080
What's gotten into you?

622
00:37:26,120 --> 00:37:26,960
Oww!

623
00:37:28,960 --> 00:37:29,920
My eyes.

624
00:37:31,120 --> 00:37:32,080
"My eyes."

625
00:37:32,400 --> 00:37:34,760
You've played tennis for years without complaining.

626
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:36,720
But one motorcycle ride and you're whining?

627
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:37,440
Hey!

628
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:40,080
I need my eyes to play tennis,

629
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:41,960
idiot.

630
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:43,520
Fine.

631
00:37:43,920 --> 00:37:45,440
Then protect your eyes

632
00:37:45,640 --> 00:37:46,600
and sit still.

633
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:50,440
You're not planning anything stupid, are you?

634
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:52,240
Why would I?

635
00:37:52,240 --> 00:37:53,160
I'd get hurt too.

636
00:37:53,160 --> 00:37:53,600
Huh?

637
00:37:54,680 --> 00:37:57,520
Or do you think I'd slam on the brakes

638
00:37:57,520 --> 00:37:58,640
just to make you hug me?

639
00:37:59,560 --> 00:38:00,240
Keep dreaming.

640
00:38:01,640 --> 00:38:02,680
Hey! Hey! Hey!!

641
00:38:05,560 --> 00:38:06,280
Oww.

642
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:10,960
Watch it.

643
00:38:11,320 --> 00:38:12,560
They just cut me off.

644
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:14,200
I didn't do it on purpose.

645
00:38:14,280 --> 00:38:15,000
Whatever.

646
00:38:16,480 --> 00:38:18,160
I told you not to do anything stupid.

647
00:38:22,120 --> 00:38:23,120
There's a lot of traffic ahead.

648
00:38:23,120 --> 00:38:24,200
Be careful.

649
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:34,720
If you lose and try to pull any tricks,

650
00:38:34,720 --> 00:38:35,960
I'll see you in court.

651
00:38:36,040 --> 00:38:36,760
When you lose,

652
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:38,200
don't you dare cheat my son.

653
00:38:38,960 --> 00:38:40,440
You already hate that boy, don't you?

654
00:38:40,560 --> 00:38:42,080
Let's settle this once and for all.

655
00:38:42,240 --> 00:38:43,280
I don't hate him.

656
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:44,840
You don't?

657
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:46,960
Sun!

658
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:47,960
I'm begging you.

659
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:50,440
If my family's shop goes out of business,

660
00:38:50,640 --> 00:38:52,280
I'll lose my chance to study abroad.

661
00:38:52,400 --> 00:38:53,040
If you want to go abroad,

662
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:54,240
then you'll just have to beat me.

663
00:38:55,120 --> 00:38:56,040
I'll take this one.

664
00:38:59,240 --> 00:39:00,160
Seriously,

665
00:39:00,160 --> 00:39:02,520
where have you been all these years?

666
00:39:02,760 --> 00:39:03,800
Well, I'm here now.

667
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:08,600
(GOT A FEVER RIGHT BEFORE THE MATCH)

668
00:39:12,360 --> 00:39:13,160
-What are you doing?

669
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:19,240
-Hey!

670
00:39:19,640 --> 00:39:21,600
-You came all the way to my house?

671
00:39:32,320 --> 00:39:38,000
SUPPORTED BY THE DEPARTMENT OF CULTURAL PROMOTION, MINISTRY OF CULTURE
